{"case_id":"T8032","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["harness_build_compatibility","new_public_api","api_protocol","ondemand_entry_point"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["simdjson_result_base<T>::value_unsafe() const&","simdjson_result_base<T>::value_unsafe() &&","simdjson_result<T>::value_unsafe() const&","simdjson_result<T>::value_unsafe() &&","simdjson::ondemand::parser::iterate(const simdjson_result<padded_string>&) &","print_json"],"reason":"S1 makes std::pair<T,error_code> a protected base of simdjson_result_base<T>, while H0 directly accesses `.first` in every `element.get<...>()` result. H0 therefore does not remain a valid consumer of the S1 result API. It also never exercises the newly public `value_unsafe()` lvalue/rvalue overloads or their required protocol of first establishing that `error()` is false. Finally, H0 only uses `simdjson::dom::parser`; it cannot reach the changed ondemand `parser::iterate(const simdjson_result<padded_string>&)` path that now calls `result.value_unsafe()`.","evidence":["S1 changes `simdjson_result_base : public std::pair<T, error_code>` to `simdjson_result_base : protected std::pair<T, error_code>`.","H0 uses `element.get<simdjson::dom::array>().first`, `element.get<simdjson::dom::object>().first`, and `.first` for all scalar getters.","S1 adds public `value_unsafe() const&` and `value_unsafe() &&` declarations and implementations to both `simdjson_result_base<T>` and `simdjson_result<T>`.","The documented contract says `value_unsafe()` is safe only when `error()` evaluates to false; H0 exercises neither that check/access sequence nor the rvalue move overload.","The changed ondemand overload replaces `result.first` with `result.value_unsafe()`, but H0 instantiates only `simdjson::dom::parser` and calls `parser.parse(Data, Size).get(elem)`."],"recommended_action":"Update H0 to consume successful getter results through `value_unsafe()` after checking `error()`, and add coverage for both const-lvalue and rvalue overloads. Add an ondemand path that constructs a `simdjson_result<padded_string>` from fuzz bytes and invokes `simdjson::ondemand::parser::iterate(const simdjson_result<padded_string>&)` for both successful and error results while respecting the accessor precondition."}
